# Slug is the primary match; a title match is the fallback. Written out
# literally: Starlark allows no `for` at module level. Two films can
# share a title (e.g. a film that appears under two Letterboxd slugs), so
# the title maps to the first slug in order -- a dict can't repeat a key.
